description:
pkix-path/src/lib.rs:1613–1635

The code collects matching parent indices into a Vec<usize> and then immediately loops over it just to set matched_via_i = true and push one PolicyNode per match.  The collect is unused for anything that requires a materialised list — neither the indices nor the count beyond 'non-empty' matter.  The whole block can be replaced without any allocation:

    let match_count = tree.iter().filter(|parent| {
        parent.depth == cert_depth - 1 && parent.expected_policy_set.contains(p_oid)
    }).count();
    let matched_via_i = match_count > 0;
    for _ in 0..match_count { new_nodes.push(...); }

Or, if the RFC 5280 intent is that at most one child per matched parent is created, simply use .any() and a single push.  Either way the Vec<usize> allocation (plus the enumerate + map step) is wasted work on the hot path inside the per-cert, per-policy loop.
